<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Dogs mate (Continued) (Mlie.DogsMate, Workshop 2441132298, after Revolus' original).

  That mod lets animals of one group mate: a Revolus.DogsMate.AnimalGroupDef whose pawnKinds list names the
  PawnKindDefs that may cross. It deduces nothing: an animal no group names cannot cross.

  MG_Horse joins the group Horse, where the mod puts the horse (1.6/Defs/CompatibleSpecies/Mammalia.xml, read
  2026-10-13): it is a horse breed, so it follows its analogue.

  The other three are not added, on purpose:
    - MG_TuSun (Pallas's cat) and the group Cat (Cat, Lynx): no domestic-cat hybrid is documented for Otocolobus.
    - MG_TiaoShu (jerboa, family Dipodidae): no group fits; the groups Squirrel, Rat and GuineaPig hold the
      vanilla animal of that family only.
    - MG_TuBoShu (marmot): a ground squirrel, but joining the group Squirrel would let it cross with the vanilla
      squirrel, which changes a vanilla animal for no biological reason.

  Only applied when that mod is active; without it this file changes nothing and logs nothing.
  PatchOperationFindMod matches the mod's display name. No load order is asked.
-->
<Patch>

	<Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
		<mods>
			<li>Dogs mate (Continued)</li>
		</mods>
		<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
			<xpath>/Defs/Revolus.DogsMate.AnimalGroupDef[defName="Horse"]/pawnKinds</xpath>
			<value>
				<li>MG_Horse</li>
			</value>
		</match>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
